From 1ba52e2c6f29ae90ef492ea3afca82e1b598c328 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Steffen Persvold <spersvold@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 14 Jun 2026 18:41:40 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] board: socfpga: forward-port Terasic DE25-Nano to u-boot
 2026.01

Adapt the DE25-Nano board support (added for the Terasic 2025.01 tree
in the preceding patch) to the Altera QPDS26.1 / u-boot 2026.01 base:

  - rework configs/socfpga_agilex5_de25_nano_defconfig for 2026.01
  - update the board DTS and -u-boot.dtsi (incl. MMC / Cadence SD-PHY)
  - add board/terasic/agilex5-de25-nano/{socfpga.c,Makefile} with
    board_early_init_f() -> socfpga_get_sys_mgr_addr(), enable
    CONFIG_BOARD_EARLY_INIT_F=y
  - drop the obsolete CONFIG_SPL_LDSCRIPT override so the SPL uses the
    generic armv8 ldscript (like the SoCDK)

System-manager base: 2026.01 moved socfpga_sysmgr_base init out of the
shared arch path (socfpga_get_managers_addr() now skips Agilex5) into
board_early_init_f(). Without it the base is 0 in u-boot proper, so
is_fpga_config_ready() and the GMAC PHY setup read the wrong registers
("FPGA not ready", no ethernet PHY).

Warm reset: the board carried a custom SPL ldscript from the 2025.01
tree (CONFIG_SPL_LDSCRIPT=...u-boot-spl-soc64.lds) that lacks the
.data_save section the generic armv8 ldscript provides. With
CONFIG_SPL_RECOVER_DATA_SECTION=y, spl_save_restore_data() therefore ran
with a zero-size region and never restored .data on the warm re-run of
the SPL, so "reboot" hung. The SoCDK dropped the custom ldscript in
2026; do the same here (BSS still lands in DDR via CONFIG_SPL_SEPARATE_BSS).

Boots Linux on the new stack; bridge enable and ethernet work in u-boot.
